Third-party code
----------------

This repository redistributes code written by other people. All of it is under
permissive licences that the AGPL can incorporate, and all of it keeps its own
notices.

Bundled in the page, and shipped in the container image:

- mpegts.js, at internal/control/assets/mpegts.js, under the Apache License
  2.0. The licence text is beside it at assets/LICENSE-mpegts.txt.
- es6-promise, by Yehuda Katz, Tom Dale, Stefan Penner and contributors, under
  the MIT licence. It is bundled inside mpegts.js rather than vendored
  separately; its notice is preserved at assets/mpegts.js.LICENSE.txt.

Linked into the binary, resolved through go.mod and pinned in go.sum:

- github.com/BurntSushi/toml, MIT, for reading the config file.
- github.com/bluenviron/gortsplib and mediacommon, MIT, for the RTSP output.
- the github.com/pion/* packages, MIT, which gortsplib builds on.
- github.com/google/uuid and golang.org/x/*, BSD.

go.mod and go.sum are the authoritative list, and each module carries its own
licence in the Go module cache. That list is deliberately not duplicated in
full here: a copy of it would rot the first time a dependency moved, and a
stale licence list is worse than none.

Nothing here is copyleft, so building or distributing reostream imposes no
obligation beyond keeping the notices above.

Prior art
---------

No code from Neolink is used here. The Baichuan protocol implementation in this
repository was written from packet captures taken against cameras on my own
network. Neolink, by thirtythreeforty and later QuantumEntangledAndy, is what
made the protocol legible in the first place, and its Wireshark dissector was a
reference throughout.
